WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:07.450
npx penthera: one command finds your framework, lockfiles and AI tooling

2
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:19.050
It checks offline by default, then asks before it installs anything

3
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:27.830
A scan of the local mock server, offline: only 127.0.0.1 is contacted

4
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:35.792
penthera ui --demo: the local dashboard on 127.0.0.1, with fake data

5
00:00:35.842 --> 00:00:38.622
Simple mode: one sentence on whether you can ship

6
00:00:38.672 --> 00:00:42.423
Each problem in plain words: what is wrong, how sure Penthera is, what to do

7
00:00:42.473 --> 00:00:51.555
Advanced mode: severity against confidence, and every finding

8
00:00:51.605 --> 00:00:58.856
The fix loop proposes one change at a time and waits for your OK

9
00:00:58.906 --> 00:01:07.875
Apply: Penthera patches, re-scans, and keeps the commit only if the fix holds

10
00:01:07.925 --> 00:01:14.963
Proof: the report for the owner, an auditor or a developer

11
00:01:15.013 --> 00:01:24.383
The owner report: what to fix first, in plain words
